--- STDOUT ---
A program to discover and format files for LLM prompting

Usage: lx [OPTIONS] [path|action]...

Arguments:
  [path]...   the file or directory to process (defaults to current dir)
  [action]... interleaved options and action flags; only -s starts a new section,
              resetting interleaved options to their defaults

Options:
  Global option:
  -c, --copy                Copy the final output to the system clipboard
  -o, --output <value>      Write the result to a file path instead of stdout
      --md                  Format output as Markdown (default)
      --xml                 Format output using XML tags (Claude optimized)
      --html                Format output as a standalone HTML 5 file
      --bare                Format output as plain concatenated text (no wrappers)
  -C, --stdout              Write output to stdout (default)
  -0, --null                Expect NUL-terminated filenames from stdin
      --prompts-dir <value> Directory containing prompt files for -P/--prompt-file
      --list-prompts        List every prompt in the library (relative<TAB>absolute) and exit
  -y, --config <value>      Load configuration from a specific YAML file
  -q, --quiet               Suppress the stats summary and logging
  -v, --verbose [value]     Set log level [possible values: debug, info, warn, error, silent]
      --stats               Force display of file/token summary to stderr
      --no-stats            Disable file/token summary footer entirely
  -V, --version             Print version information and exit
  -h, --help                Show help (use --help for detailed documentation)

  Interleaved option:
  -l, --line-numbers        Enable line numbers for subsequent files
  -n, --lines <n>           Limit subsequent files to N lines (0 for compact)
      --head <n>            Read only the first N lines of subsequent files
      --tail <n>            Read only the last N lines of subsequent files
  -i, --include <value>     Add a glob whitelist pattern to subsequent files
  -e, --exclude <value>     Add a glob blacklist pattern to subsequent files
  -m, --max-size <size>     Skip files larger than the given size for subsequent paths
  -D, --documents           Extract text from document files for subsequent paths
  -M, --media               Describe media files by their metadata for subsequent paths
  -Z, --expand              Expand archive files inline for subsequent paths
  -H, --hidden              Include hidden files (dotfiles) for subsequent paths
  -S, --follow              Follow directory symlinks for subsequent paths
      --no-links            Skip symbolic links to files for subsequent paths
  -I, --no-ignore           Disable .gitignore filtering for subsequent paths
  -u, --functions           Show only function/method signatures for subsequent files
  -Y, --types               Show only type/class definitions for subsequent files

  Action:
  -T, --tree                Print file tree for the section (with content)
  -t, --tree-only           Print a file tree for the section (no content)
  -f, --file <value>        Force process a specific path (bypasses ignores/filters)
  -s, --section <value>     Insert a logical separator with a header
  -E, --system-context      Insert a block describing the machine and invocation
  -p, --prompt <value>      Inject a custom text prompt into the output
  -P, --prompt-file <value> Load a prompt by name from the prompts library, or from a path

--- STDERR ---
